            <hr />

            <h2>Mission and Philosophy: Preventative Jurisprudence</h2>
            <p>
              The core thesis of <em>Legal Kit ni Juan</em> is built upon the
              author's conviction that true leadership in the legal sphere must
              involve listening, serving, and educating the populace. Atty.
              Sorongon observed a recurring pattern: a vast majority of
              agonizing cases could have been circumvented if the individuals
              involved had possessed baseline knowledge from the beginning.
            </p>
            <p>
              The prevailing cultural norm in the Philippines dictates that
              legal intervention is a desperate, final resort—an action taken
              only when one is already facing imminent termination, foreclosure,
              or physical harm. At this late stage, individuals have often
              already unwittingly waived critical rights or destroyed vital
              evidence. The book seeks to cure this by establishing
              <strong>preventative jurisprudence</strong>.
            </p>

            <hr />

            <h2>A Comprehensive Taxonomy of Crucial Rights</h2>
            <p>
              The guide meticulously identifies specific spheres of daily life
              where rights are frequently violated, culturally ignored, or
              misunderstood by victims.
            </p>

            <table>
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>Domain of Friction</th>
                  <th>Nature of Right Violated</th>
                  <th>Cultural Context & Misconception</th>
                  <th>Legal Matrix Addressed</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>Labor & Workplace</strong></td>
                  <td>Unpaid wages, illegal dismissal, denial of benefits.</td>
                  <td>
                    Emphasis on <em>utang na loob</em> (gratitude) prohibits
                    workers from demanding compensation.
                  </td>
                  <td>
                    Assertion of rights under the Labor Code and combating
                    illegal termination.
                  </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>Community Relations</strong></td>
                  <td>
